Subject: [PATCH] Real TBC case: a company role's name on LinkedIn is a source
 for the officeholder gate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's box 60161 (Lika's goal, threads 52471 and 52475): „ნათია
ფაჩიკაშვილი — Director of MSME Banking" came from a LinkedIn post in the
search results, and the gate replaced the name with „(სახელი ვერ დავადასტურე
ოფიციალურ გვერდზე)", twice in one answer — a search snippet was never
evidence. Misho, 15 Oct: LinkedIn counts as a source. The LinkedIn hits of a
web search are kept as their own evidence and pass a name in a sentence about
a company role; a public office (minister, mayor, ambassador …) is still
checked only against pages the run read, and other sites' snippets still are
not evidence.

